# Panel 180 R5, shape 31 of the compiler-engineer's 117 (call args): a break
# before . in an argument.
# By the spec's opening paragraph, the line ends with `xs`, a name, so it
# keeps its NEWLINE, which may stand only before a closing bracket or a `,`,
# or where a production writes it, and none writes it before `.`: refused,
# exit 1.
function main()
    f(xs
        .len())  #~ line_end_before_continuation
